From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 22:06:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add DKIM2 Message-Instance header support

Record what the list changed, per draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-06, so a
downstream verifier can undo Sympa's changes and check the signatures of
earlier hops.

At ingress (ProcessIncoming), before any modification: if the message
carries no Message-Instance, add m=1 describing it as received; if it
carries one (from an inbound milter or a signing sender) leave it alone
and record which state it describes. The original is kept as a .mi_orig
file beside the message in the outgoing spool, hard-linked between spool
entries for the same message, bridging the process boundary between
sympa_msg.pl and bulk.pl.

At egress (ProcessOutgoing), after all transformations and before DKIM
signing: verify the incoming top instance against the original (skip MI
entirely if it does not match, rather than build on a broken chain), then
compare the hashes; if nothing changed add no header, otherwise add the
next m= with header and body Recipes rebuilding the original. Internally
generated messages, resent archive messages and direct sends through
ToMailer get an originating m=1. Digests are skipped.

Mail::DKIM2::MessageInstance (from the dkim2wg/interop Perl library) is a
soft dependency: without it no header is added.

The wire format follows the draft: m= numbers the instance, h= carries
"alg:header-hash:body-hash", r= the base64 JSON Recipe. DKIM2_DRAFT and
DKIM2_DATE in Sympa::Message name the draft implemented and the date of
the last change to what is emitted.

Includes DKIM2-MESSAGE-INSTANCE.md (design and resource impact) and
t/Message_DKIM2.t, wired into Makefile.am's check_SCRIPTS: instance
creation, preservation of upstream instances, multi-hop chains,
skip-if-unchanged, encoding preservation, spool hard linking and full
round-trip verify/undo.

